{title: Nine Little Fruits}
{subtitle: Galatians 5:22–23}
{key: C}
{tempo: 114}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [F] [G] | [C] |
| [F] [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Love says I will share my [G]bread
[Dm7]Joy goes jumping on a[C]head
Peace sits quiet, calm and [F]still
[G]Patience waits and [C]always will
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The fruit of the Spirit is [F]love, joy, [G]peace
[C]Patience, kindness, [F]goodness, faithful[G]ness
[C]Gentleness, [F]self-con-[G]trol
A[C]gainst such [G]things there [C]is no law
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Kindness helps a friend who [G]falls
[Dm]Goodness does what is right for [C]all
Faithful keeps the words it [F]said
[G]Gentle tucks the [C]lamb in bed
[F]Self-con-trol says stop and wait
[G]Take a breath and count to eight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [C]fruit of the Spirit is [F]love, joy, [G]peace
[C]Patience, kindness, [F]goodness, faithful[G]ness
[C]Gentleness, [F]self-con-[G]trol
A[C]gainst such [G]things there [C]is no law
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[F]Nine little fruits on the Spir[C]it tree
[G]Growing in you [C]and growing in me
[F]One, two, three, four, [C]five, six, seven, eight, [G]nine
Growing in you and [C]growing in me
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Love, joy, [F]peace
[C]Patience, kindness, [F]goodness, faithful[G]ness
[C]Gentleness, [F]self-con-[G]trol [C]
{end_of_verse}
